SUMMARY:Panigiri and pilgrimage of Agia Marina\, Voni
LOCATION:Voni\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The monastery of Agia Marina at Voni in the Pediada is Crete's main Agia Marina pilgrimage: from the evening of 16 July queues of pilgrims stretch out of the two churches (the tiny old one and the big new one)\, people sleep in the courtyard to fulfil vows\, and stalls and a glenti fill the road outside. Come on the eve for the atmosphere\; the morning liturgy on the 17th is packed and parking is a kilometre away on the Kastelli road.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#voni-panigiri-and-pilgrimage-of-agia-marina-voni
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#voni-panigiri-and-pilgrimage-of-agia-marina-voni
